+// Whether a noised half-transparent pixel survives what a page does with it:
+// unpremultiplied by getImageData or the PNG, premultiplied again when that PNG
+// is drawn onto another canvas, and read back. A channel exactly between two
+// unpremultiplied values is left alone too, since GPU and CPU readbacks round
+// that one differently. Unchecked, 20 such pixels of a line of text read back
+// changed from their own PNG, which real Chrome never does and BrowserScan
+// tests (issue 46, measured on core 158, 26.11.2026).
+inline bool RoundTrips(int c, int a) {
+  return (c * 255 % a) * 2 != a && Premul(Unpremul(c, a), a) == c;
